# Theme system – token-only colors

This project uses a **token-based theming system**. Dark/Light mode is controlled by `[data-theme="dark"]` and `[data-theme="light"]` on `<html>`.

## Rule

- **Do NOT** use hardcoded Tailwind color classes for backgrounds, text, or borders in shared UI (e.g. `bg-white`, `bg-slate-800`, `text-gray-500`, `border-slate-600`).
- **Do** use theme token classes from `resources/css/theme.css`.

## Token classes (use these)

| Purpose | Class |
|--------|--------|
| Page background | `theme-bg-primary` |
| Cards / panels | `theme-card-bg` or `theme-card-bg-only` |
| Sidebar | `theme-sidebar-bg`, `theme-sidebar-text`, `theme-sidebar-link-hover`, `theme-sidebar-active` |
| Navbar | `theme-navbar-bg` |
| Text | `theme-text-primary`, `theme-text-secondary`, `theme-text-muted` |
| Borders | `theme-border` |
| Buttons | `theme-btn-primary`, `theme-btn-secondary` |
| Status | `theme-status-success-bg`, `theme-status-danger-bg`, `theme-status-warning-bg`, `theme-status-info-bg` |
| Modals / dropdowns | `theme-modal-bg`, `theme-modal-backdrop`, `theme-dropdown-bg` |
| Tables | `theme-table-header-bg`, `theme-table-row-hover`, `theme-table-border` |
| Inputs | `theme-input-bg`, `theme-input-border`, `theme-input-placeholder`, `theme-input-focus` |
| Body | `theme-body` |

## Allowed exceptions

- Accent gradients (e.g. logo `from-cyan-400 to-orange-500`) and status badges that stay semantic (e.g. `border-emerald-500/30` for success borders).
- Third-party vendor views where changing would require forking heavily.

## Adding new UI

When adding new Blade views or components, use only the token classes above so the UI respects the user’s theme (Admin, Client, Developer, Sales, Guest).
